			<div id="breadcrumb">
				<div class="container">
					

<a href="/"><i aria-label="Home" class="gs-home"> </i></a>

            <i aria-hidden="true" class="gs-right-pointing-arrow"> </i>
                <span>
    
            Athletics
    
</span>
    

				</div>
			</div>
			                 <section class="page-content block">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="block-container">
                                        <p><p><a href="https://gscathletics.com/landing/index"></a>Athletics offer a variety of benefits and enhancements both at the academic and student engagement levels. Gordon State College offers both <strong>Intercollegiate</strong> and&#160;<strong>Club Sports</strong>&#160;for students interested in athletic competition. &#160;</p>
<p><a href="https://gscathletics.com/landing/index" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong><i>Intercollegiate Sports</i></strong></a>&#160;are regulated by the National Junior Athletic Association (NJCAA) and have varsity status.&#160; The NJCAA recognizes the diverse nature of its membership, providing at all times a consistent and inclusive governance structure that provides opportunities for all stakeholders and emphasizes the academic, athletic, and community involvement goals for all student-athletes. Intercollegiate teams are highly competitive and require a significant time commitment from the athletes.</p>
<p><strong><i><a href="https://www.gordonstate.edu/student-life/health-recreation/recreation/club-sports/index.html">Club Sports</a> </i></strong>are not regulated by any intercollegiate association such as the&#160;NJCAA and do not have varsity status.&#160;Although&#160;club sports&#160;may&#160;not&#160;be&#160;as competitive as intercollegiate sports, they offer college athletes the ability to play at a competitive level without the time commitment generally required&#160;for a sport governed by the NJCAA.&#160;Since&#160;club sports consist of teams that are not affiliated with an&#160;intercollegiate association,&#160;these teams&#160;are supported by student activities, club advisors, student leaders,&#160;volunteers, and may be funded by participants through club fees.</p></p>
                
                            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
        
    
